msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:289
msgid "Your account"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:290
msgid "Your profile, dark mode, and <strong>Replay the tutorial</strong> — this tour is always one click away from here."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:299
msgid "The page header"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:300
msgid "Every screen opens with the same header: where you are, how many records matched, and the actions available on them."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:310
msgid "Page actions"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:311
msgid "The buttons that act on what you are looking at. They change from screen to screen, but always sit here."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:324
msgid "Free-text search across the list. It is on every index in MISP, and the term is kept in the URL — a search can be bookmarked or sent to a colleague as a link."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:335 View/Elements/view_event_graph.ctp:9
#: View/Events/index.ctp:150 View/Servers/preview_index.ctp:42
#: View/TaxiiServers/index.ctp:74 View/TaxiiServers/view.ctp:47
#: View/Themed/Overmind/SharingGroupBlueprints/add.ctp:98
#: View/Themed/Overmind/Sightings/ajax/advanced.ctp:109
#: View/Themed/UiBeta/Events/index.ctp:222
msgid "Filters"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:336
msgid "Narrow the list by the fields that matter for it — distribution, threat level, organisation. Filters stack with the search rather than replacing it."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:347
#: View/Themed/Overmind/Elements/Logs/pager_prevnext.ctp:8
#: View/Themed/Overmind/Elements/genericElementsBS5/IndexTable/pagination_nav.ctp:19
msgid "Pagination"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:348
msgid "How many records matched and where you are in them. The same controls sit at the top of the list, so you never have to scroll back up to turn a page."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:359
msgid "Table or cards"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:360
msgid "The same data, two densities: a table for scanning many rows at once, cards for reading fewer in more detail. Your choice is remembered."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:371
msgid "A row"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:372
msgid "One record per row, with its key fields as columns. Sort by any column from its header, and double-click a row to open it."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:386
msgid "The actions column"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:387
msgid "The last column holds what you can do to that record — view, edit, delete — and only shows the actions your permissions allow, so it is shorter for some accounts than others."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:407
msgid "Report an incident"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:410
msgid "The end-to-end path: open an event, fill it, classify it, then share it."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:416
msgid "Create the event and feed it"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:421
msgid "Classify it"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:426
msgid "Share and publish it"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:442
msgid "Start a new event"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:443
msgid "Go ahead and click <strong>Add Event</strong>. The tour follows you into the dialog."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:451
msgid "Name the event"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:452
msgid "One line describing what happened — this is what your colleagues read first in the event list."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:454
msgid "Be specific: &ldquo;Phishing campaign impersonating ACME invoices&rdquo; beats &ldquo;phishing&rdquo;."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:462
msgid "Who gets to see it"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:463
msgid "Distribution decides how far the event travels: your organisation only, this community, connected communities, everyone, or a named sharing group."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:466
msgid "It is the single most important field on this form — it is what stops sensitive data leaving your org."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:474 View/Themed/Overmind/Events/add.ctp:160
msgid "Analysis level"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:475
msgid "How far along your own investigation is. Start at <strong>Initial</strong> and raise it as the picture firms up — recipients use it to judge how much to trust the event."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:485
msgid "How dangerous this is to the people receiving it. It drives triage on the other side, so keep it honest."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:503
msgid "Create it"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:504
msgid "Submit the form. MISP opens the new event and the tour picks up there."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:511
msgid "Create your event to carry on — the tutorial resumes on the event page."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:513
msgid "Inside an event"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:514
msgid "An event is empty until you feed it. These tabs hold its attributes, objects, reports and correlations — the counters tell you what is already there."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:523
msgid "Quick actions"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:524
msgid "Everything you can do to this event in one column: add data, populate it from a report, export it, publish it."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:535
msgid "Add your first attribute"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:536
msgid "Click <strong>Add Attribute</strong> to record a single indicator — a hash, a domain, an IP address."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:545
msgid "What role the indicator plays: network activity, payload delivery, artefacts dropped, and so on. The category narrows the types offered next."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:555
msgid "The concrete kind of value — <code>md5</code>, <code>domain</code>, <code>ip-src</code>. Type is what lets MISP correlate your indicator against everyone else&rsquo;s."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:566
msgid "The indicator itself. You can paste several at once and tick batch import to create one attribute per line."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:574
msgid "Actionable or context?"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:575
msgid "<strong>IDS</strong> marks an attribute as safe to push into detection tools. Leave it off for context that would generate false positives — a legitimate domain an attacker abused, for instance."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:587
msgid "The fast way to feed an event"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:588
msgid "Typing indicators one at a time gets old. <strong>Populate from</strong> takes a whole report, finds the indicators in it and proposes them in bulk for you to accept."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:599
msgid "Where it all lands"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:600
msgid "Whatever you add shows up under <strong>Attributes</strong>, where you can filter, edit and export it."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:619;692
msgid "Open any event"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:620
msgid "Classification happens on an event, so pick one from the list — any will do."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:627
msgid "Open an event to carry on with classification."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:630
msgid "Tags come from <strong>taxonomies</strong> — agreed vocabularies rather than free text. <code>tlp:amber</code> means the same thing to every MISP user, which is exactly why tags are worth more than notes."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:642
msgid "Apply a tag"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:643
msgid "Open the tag picker. Start with a <code>tlp:</code> tag — it states how far the recipient may pass the event on."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:651
msgid "The tag picker"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:652
msgid "Search across every enabled taxonomy, then select the tags to apply. Local tags stay on your instance and are never shared onward."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:663
msgid "Where tags label an event, galaxies connect it to known things: threat actors, malware families, ATT&amp;CK techniques."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:666
msgid "Attach the right cluster and your event joins everything else attributed to that actor."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:674
msgid "Attach a cluster"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:675
msgid "The picker searches every galaxy at once. There are tens of thousands of clusters, so type a name rather than browsing."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:693
msgid "Sharing is decided per event, so open one to see the controls in place."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:700
msgid "Open an event to carry on with sharing and publication."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:702
msgid "Distribution, in place"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:703
msgid "The event&rsquo;s distribution is shown here, and each attribute carries its own. An attribute is never shared more widely than the event that holds it, so the event level is the ceiling."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:712
msgid "Before you publish"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:713
msgid "Publishing is not a save button. Check the distribution and the tags first — an unpublished event stays with your organisation."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:727
msgid "Publishing marks the event as ready and hands it to everyone its distribution allows — connected instances pull it, and subscribers may be emailed."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:730
msgid "You can unpublish afterwards, but you cannot recall what has already been pulled. Treat it as a one-way door."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:748
msgid "The shared vocabularies: taxonomies, galaxies and the lists that keep noise out."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:754
msgid "Tags and taxonomies"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:759
msgid "Where vocabularies live"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:760
msgid "Everything in this section sits under <strong>Data models</strong>. If a tag you want does not exist, its taxonomy is probably just not enabled yet."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:770
#: View/DecayingModel/decaying_tool_basescore.ctp:13
#: View/Taxonomies/index.ctp:3
#: View/Themed/Overmind/Taxonomies/ajax/taxonomyEnableAllTagsConfirmationForm.ctp:14
msgid "Taxonomies"
msgstr "อนุกรมวิธาน"

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:771
msgid "A taxonomy is a published vocabulary — TLP, PAP, the admiralty scale. Enabling one makes its tags available across the instance."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:775
msgid "Tagging from a taxonomy rather than inventing labels is what makes events searchable across organisations."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:784
msgid "Finding one"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:785
msgid "There are well over a hundred. Search by name, then open one to enable it and pick which of its tags you want exposed."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:796
msgid "The resulting tags"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:797
msgid "Every tag available on this instance, taxonomy-backed or custom, with how often each one is used."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:812
msgid "Galaxies and clusters"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:813
msgid "A galaxy is a catalogue of known things — threat actors, malware, ATT&amp;CK techniques, sectors. Each entry is a <strong>cluster</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:817
msgid "Attaching a cluster to an event is how attribution gets recorded in a way other instances understand."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:826
msgid "Keeping them current"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:827
msgid "Galaxies ship from the community repository and are updated in place, so clusters stay in step with what the rest of the ecosystem uses."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:836
msgid "Filters and lists"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:843
msgid "Warning lists"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:844
msgid "Lists of values that are almost certainly not malicious — public DNS resolvers, top-ranked domains, RFC1918 ranges."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:847
msgid "MISP flags attributes that hit one instead of blocking them, so you keep the data but see the warning."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:858
msgid "Notice lists"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:859
msgid "The advisory counterpart: they attach guidance to matching data — legal or handling notes an analyst should read before acting."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:878
msgid "Sync and feeds"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:881
msgid "Where intelligence comes in from, where yours goes, and who you share it with."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:893
msgid "Two ways data arrives"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:894
msgid "<strong>Feeds</strong> pull from a URL or a file. <strong>Servers</strong> are two-way links to other MISP instances. Both live under Sync."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:905
msgid "One-way sources of indicators, in MISP or CSV format. Enable one and its data becomes searchable; cache it and you can correlate against it without importing everything."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:916
msgid "Adding a source"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:917
msgid "Add a feed by URL, or import a whole set of feed definitions at once. The default list ships with MISP."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:926
msgid "Remote servers"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:932
msgid "Sync servers"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:933
msgid "Other MISP instances you exchange with. Each link says whether you pull from it, push to it, or both."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:936
msgid "This list is the honest answer to &ldquo;who receives what I publish?&rdquo;."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:945
msgid "Before trusting a link"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:946
msgid "A new connection can be tested before it carries anything — MISP checks the credentials and reports what the remote end would accept."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:955;962
#: View/Themed/Overmind/Galaxies/export.ctp:45
#: View/Themed/Overmind/Organisations/view.ctp:59
msgid "Sharing groups"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:963
msgid "When the fixed distribution levels are too blunt, a sharing group names exactly which organisations may see an event."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:966
msgid "Pick &ldquo;Sharing group&rdquo; as an event&rsquo;s distribution and this is the list you choose from."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:988
msgid "Users, organisations, roles and the instance settings behind them."
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:994
msgid "Users and organisations"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:999
msgid "The admin menu"
msgstr ""

#: Lib/Tools/OnboardingTour.php:1000
msgid "Accounts, organisations, roles and instance settings all hang off this menu. What you see in it depends on whether you administer your own organisation or the whole instance."
msgstr ""

